WEBVTT

00:08.960 --> 00:13.480
<b><i>Now I know exactly how it 
feels to want a new job...</i></b>

00:14.010 --> 00:20.280
<b>The High Leadership is beginning serious 
discussions about conquering Ildoa.</b>

00:20.740 --> 00:25.580
<b><i>The brass is taking a reckless gamble 
to avoid dying by slow attrition.</i></b>

00:25.580 --> 00:27.740
<b><i>Now they risk us all 
getting totally screwed.</i></b>

00:28.540 --> 00:31.650
<b><i>So now they're daydreaming 
when they should be trying to fight a war?</i></b>

00:31.650 --> 00:33.000
<b><i>Screw that.</i></b>

00:33.780 --> 00:36.250
<b><i>The problem is how to leave.</i></b>

00:37.060 --> 00:41.260
<b><i>It's hard to accept an ending that 
would leave Being X laughing at me.</i></b>

00:41.590 --> 00:45.550
<b><i>But I refuse to become 
a sacrificial lamb.</i></b>

00:45.550 --> 00:48.450
<b><i>So what the hell do I do?</i></b>

02:18.990 --> 02:21.740
<b>July 25th, Unified Year 1927</b>

02:19.980 --> 02:21.750
<b>We've finished our analysis 
of the proposal.</b>

02:22.370 --> 02:25.480
<b>As we thought, there is no chance 
of an invasion of Ildoa succeeding.</b>

02:25.480 --> 02:27.300
<b>The best we could do</b>

02:25.580 --> 02:30.460
This story is a work of fiction. People, organizations, locations, laws, names, etc. have no relation to any real-life counterparts.

02:27.300 --> 02:30.490
<b>is launch a strategic surprise attack, 
betting everything on the initial battle,</b>

02:30.760 --> 02:34.610
<b>and wipe out their field army 
near our border.</b>

02:34.610 --> 02:39.000
<b>Assuming this worked, we could blitz our 
way down and conquer northern Ildoa.</b>

02:39.000 --> 02:40.770
<b>We couldn't go any further.</b>

02:41.300 --> 02:47.480
<b>And this is assuming every possible 
thing breaks in our favor, yes?</b>

02:47.480 --> 02:51.160
<b>Yes. Even under the most 
optimistic assumptions,</b>

02:51.160 --> 02:54.080
<b>our troops don't make it 
further than northern Ildoa.</b>

02:54.470 --> 02:56.820
<b>And so the idea of reducing 
the Ildoan threat to the south,</b>

02:56.820 --> 02:59.660
<b>and reallocating the troops 
stationed there to the east,</b>

02:59.660 --> 03:01.840
<b>is just downright fantasy?</b>

03:01.840 --> 03:02.990
<b>Yes.</b>

03:03.550 --> 03:07.840
<b>But our troops are pinned 
down already, yes?</b>

03:08.110 --> 03:10.570
<b>By Ildoa's breach of trust.</b>

03:11.840 --> 03:14.830
<b>That dumbass Zettour is 
having trouble in the east.</b>

03:14.830 --> 03:17.380
<b>I'd like to help him out.</b>

03:17.610 --> 03:23.420
<b>I'm afraid pulling troops from 
the Ildoan border is... difficult.</b>

03:23.420 --> 03:27.940
<b>I know. They're intent on 
refusing to take a side.</b>

03:28.400 --> 03:32.020
<b>They talk so much about 
how we're friends and allies,</b>

03:32.020 --> 03:34.000
<b>but they refused to allow 
our retreating troops</b>

03:34.000 --> 03:36.270
<b>from the south 
passage through their territory.</b>

03:36.270 --> 03:38.970
<b>I hate them so much.</b>

03:39.280 --> 03:44.800
<b>Ildoa is a neutral country, intent on 
putting their own interests first.</b>

03:45.570 --> 03:50.390
<b>As long as the Empire is in a stalemate,
it's willing to be a good neighbor.</b>

03:52.290 --> 03:55.350
<b>But what if we're too weak to fight?</b>

03:55.350 --> 03:58.090
<b>What will they do then?</b>

03:58.510 --> 03:59.960
<b>If I may, sir,</b>

03:59.960 --> 04:04.170
<b>the Ildoans seem more likely 
to talk than fight.</b>

04:05.550 --> 04:10.970
<b>We can talk to Ildoa. So we can find a 
way to survive through dialogue, then.</b>

04:11.490 --> 04:12.560
<b>Yes.</b>

04:13.510 --> 04:18.160
<b>But part of a strategic officer's job 
is to prepare for the worst case.</b>

04:18.160 --> 04:20.080
<b>We must prepare for both peace and war.</b>

04:20.850 --> 04:24.770
<b>And which shall we prioritize: 
peace or war?</b>

04:27.190 --> 04:33.760
<b>We'll have to maximize our efforts at 
diplomacy with the time we have left.</b>

04:34.360 --> 04:39.540
<b>Do you know how many frontline troops
will die while we waste our time talking?</b>

04:39.990 --> 04:42.700
<b>There's no time to waste.</b>

04:42.920 --> 04:44.440
<b>You're correct.</b>

04:44.840 --> 04:48.930
<b>We need to find an exit, 
and we need to do it now.</b>

04:48.930 --> 04:53.190
<b>There's a new counselor in the Foreign 
Affairs ministry named Konrad.</b>

04:53.640 --> 04:58.060
<b>The ministry has just done a major 
reorganization. I want you to help him.</b>

04:58.060 --> 04:59.510
<b>Yes, I'll get to it immediately.</b>

05:00.960 --> 05:03.330
<b>We have limited time left.</b>

05:03.330 --> 05:06.160
<b>So I want you to give this your all.</b>

05:06.150 --> 05:08.910
<b>Episode Ten
A Way to Survive</b>

05:11.910 --> 05:17.420
<b>Imperial Foreign Affairs Ministry</b>

05:12.650 --> 05:14.780
<b>I apologize for the sudden summons.</b>

05:14.780 --> 05:17.410
<b>No, I can understand, 
given the situation.</b>

05:17.730 --> 05:21.880
<b>There's no need to be diplomatic during 
your discussion with the foreign ministry.</b>

05:21.880 --> 05:23.370
<b>Don't hold back.</b>

05:23.370 --> 05:24.200
<b>Understood, sir.</b>

05:29.090 --> 05:34.080
<b>Thank you for inviting us today, 
Counselor Konrad.</b>

05:33.560 --> 05:40.230
<b>Imperial Foreign Affairs Ministry
Counselor Konrad</b>

05:34.980 --> 05:37.580
<b>Hello, Colonel Rerugen.</b>

05:37.580 --> 05:40.230
<b>And who is this young lady?</b>

05:40.230 --> 05:42.770
<b>Lieutenant Colonel Tanya von Degurechaff.</b>

05:42.770 --> 05:45.480
<b>She's here due to her deep understanding
 of the frontline situation.</b>

05:45.480 --> 05:48.350
<b>She's a hero, a recipient 
of the Silver Wings medal.</b>

05:48.350 --> 05:51.120
<b>Oh, my deepest apologies.</b>

05:51.120 --> 05:53.320
<b>No, it's fine.</b>

05:53.690 --> 05:57.190
<b>We are servants of the Imperial nation.</b>

05:57.190 --> 06:00.400
<b>I hope we can work well together.</b>

06:02.360 --> 06:04.130
<b>Now, let me just ask it bluntly.</b>

06:04.430 --> 06:06.780
<b>Can we win this war?</b>

06:06.780 --> 06:08.900
<b>I want to hear your answer directly.</b>

06:09.370 --> 06:13.600
<b><i>Even directly, I can't tell him that 
all our sacrifices were meaningless,</i></b>

06:13.600 --> 06:14.760
<b><i>and we can't win.</i></b>

06:14.760 --> 06:16.960
<b>Nope. Not a chance.</b>

06:16.960 --> 06:19.880
<b>I can tell you right now that 
there's no point in continuing.</b>

06:20.900 --> 06:23.400
<b>Isn't that a little too pessimistic?</b>

06:23.400 --> 06:25.980
<b>You'd prefer total victory?</b>

06:25.980 --> 06:28.710
<b>Go find a con man and 
ask his opinion, then.</b>

06:28.710 --> 06:32.710
<b>Any soldier with half a brain 
would tell you the same thing.</b>

06:33.150 --> 06:36.000
<b>You're speaking on behalf of 
the entire army, at your age?</b>

06:36.290 --> 06:38.190
<b>Her appearance aside,</b>

06:38.190 --> 06:42.600
<b>Lt. Colonel Degurechaff is a talented
soldier with a history of achievement.</b>

06:42.600 --> 06:45.920
<b>Though I admit she could've said it 
a bit more diplomatically.</b>

06:46.460 --> 06:49.690
<b>I see. Perhaps I'm being stubborn.</b>

06:50.170 --> 06:52.000
<b>What evidence do you have, if I may ask?</b>

06:52.270 --> 06:54.330
<b>The Imperial Army is strong,</b>

06:54.330 --> 06:58.440
<b>but not strong enough to defeat 
every army in the world.</b>

06:58.650 --> 07:01.650
<b>We defeated the Republic 
and the Entente Alliance,</b>

07:01.650 --> 07:06.370
<b>but the Federation and 
the Allied Kingdom remain threats.</b>

07:06.760 --> 07:10.240
<b>And we can't ignore the possibility of
 the Unified States joining the fray.</b>

07:10.240 --> 07:12.480
<b>There are enemies everywhere you look.</b>

07:12.790 --> 07:15.630
<b>We can't win this war anymore.</b>

07:15.630 --> 07:19.530
<b>I believe it follows logically that we'll 
be trapped with no exit until we're dead.</b>

07:21.320 --> 07:22.950
<b>An exit.</b>

07:22.950 --> 07:26.050
<b>And you seek to find 
that through diplomacy?</b>

07:26.490 --> 07:29.610
<b>Though it brings shame to our military 
for not being able to win...</b>

07:29.610 --> 07:30.710
<b>That's correct.</b>

07:31.130 --> 07:33.810
<b>We're at the point where 
we need to cut our losses.</b>

07:33.810 --> 07:37.810
<b>So a soldier back from the front lines 
is allowed to say all this?</b>

07:37.810 --> 07:42.760
<b>Colonel Rerugen, I'm quite impressed 
with our Imperial Army's education.</b>

07:43.220 --> 07:46.610
<b><i>This monster grew up without me 
teaching her a thing, actually...</i></b>

07:47.360 --> 07:49.060
<b>But Lieutenant Colonel,</b>

07:49.060 --> 07:52.240
<b>even if we're cutting our losses, 
there are lines we don't want to cross.</b>

07:52.240 --> 07:55.880
<b>How much, in the military's estimation, 
should we be willing to accept?</b>

07:58.030 --> 08:01.590
<b><i>To be honest, I'm not sure 
how to answer that.</i></b>

08:01.950 --> 08:04.370
<b><i>Unfortunately, opinions differ 
even on the front lines.</i></b>

08:04.900 --> 08:07.010
<b><i>"In my estimation..."</i></b>

08:07.830 --> 08:10.660
<b><i>we're not as stubborn as the public.</i></b>

08:10.660 --> 08:14.880
<b><i>But there are few organizations who 
value their dead as much as the military.</i></b>

08:15.330 --> 08:19.760
<b><i>But there's also no point in wasting 
time and then surrendering...</i></b>

08:20.640 --> 08:22.990
<b><i>The whole Empire could fall.</i></b>

08:23.700 --> 08:28.270
<b><i>If we accept that, we should be able 
to give up on pretty much anything.</i></b>

08:28.790 --> 08:31.930
<b>I'm simply a field officer.</b>

08:31.930 --> 08:35.990
<b>There are rules about what I can say 
when it comes to the strategic picture...</b>

08:35.990 --> 08:39.630
<b>Lieutenant Colonel, I'd like 
your opinion anyway.</b>

08:39.630 --> 08:42.160
<b>Could you give us something 
to start with?</b>

08:42.160 --> 08:43.630
<b>Colonel?</b>

08:43.630 --> 08:47.870
<b>All the High Leadership gives us 
is wishful thinking.</b>

08:48.170 --> 08:51.480
<b>But even Strategic HQ can't come 
to an opinion on the matter.</b>

09:01.320 --> 09:03.100
<b>What a coincidence.</b>

09:03.100 --> 09:06.690
<b>We aren't that different ourselves.</b>

09:07.400 --> 09:11.930
<b>So nobody in the bureaucracy 
agrees about what to do, either?</b>

09:14.440 --> 09:18.690
<b>Ridiculous factional infighting 
and half-hearted populism...</b>

09:19.170 --> 09:24.220
<b>We don't have time to work our way 
out of all the layers of restraint</b>

09:24.220 --> 09:26.610
<b>that our predecessors 
put on us, I suppose.</b>

09:27.700 --> 09:30.420
<b>So why don't we just do it ourselves?</b>

09:30.640 --> 09:33.800
<b>We can present our results to 
the Empire as a fait accompli.</b>

09:34.240 --> 09:38.260
<b>We'll have the military negotiate 
with Ildoa at the officer level.</b>

09:38.260 --> 09:40.880
<b>We tried that with Ildoa, and failed.</b>

09:40.880 --> 09:44.970
<b>And we were told to go win some more 
fights to get better conditions.</b>

09:44.970 --> 09:49.140
<b>And that's why you're here, 
or did you forget?</b>

09:49.530 --> 09:53.960
<b>I'm here because my predecessor 
got his ass fired.</b>

09:53.960 --> 09:57.220
<b>Every organization wants 
results, not just yours.</b>

09:57.830 --> 09:58.990
<b>You're saying...</b>

10:00.910 --> 10:03.330
<b>I'll spread the word, quietly.</b>

10:03.330 --> 10:07.450
<b>If things get worse, someone's going to 
have to take responsibility for that.</b>

10:07.730 --> 10:10.120
<b>But in the strictest sense, 
isn't that illegal?</b>

10:10.860 --> 10:12.880
<b>Colonel, it's against regulations</b>

10:12.880 --> 10:16.760
<b>for the military to get involved in 
the ministry's internal matters.</b>

10:16.760 --> 10:20.530
<b>But we have a duty to advise the nation,</b>

10:20.530 --> 10:25.300
<b>and we certainly have the right 
to make any proposal we wish...</b>

10:29.030 --> 10:30.290
<b>Yes.</b>

10:30.290 --> 10:33.800
<b>It's just one of those little tricks 
we bureaucrats have.</b>

10:33.800 --> 10:36.590
<b>External diplomacy requires 
internal diplomacy as well.</b>

10:36.590 --> 10:40.660
<b>No diplomatic effort can succeed 
without internal preparations.</b>

10:41.810 --> 10:43.870
<b>We need an exit, no matter the cost.</b>

10:43.870 --> 10:47.050
<b>And I want you to know that for that,</b>

10:47.050 --> 10:51.120
<b>I'll need to ask you to propose 
compromises that are humiliating.</b>

10:52.500 --> 10:54.500
<b>August 2nd, Unified Year 1927</b>

10:55.420 --> 10:57.540
<b>Out of the question! Absurd!</b>

10:57.540 --> 11:00.180
<b>Our military should not be 
offering these conditions!</b>

11:00.180 --> 11:02.090
<b>Or are you saying we should surrender?</b>

11:02.090 --> 11:06.340
<b>If this draft ever sees the light 
of day, there'll be public uproar!</b>

11:06.340 --> 11:08.230
<b>What do we tell the fallen?!</b>

11:08.230 --> 11:10.280
<b>Don't you care about the Empire's honor?</b>

11:10.280 --> 11:10.930
<b>This is treason!</b>

11:10.930 --> 11:12.270
<b>You're just a defeatist!</b>

11:14.580 --> 11:20.580
<b>Under present conditions, we need 
to be brave enough to find an exit,</b>

11:20.580 --> 11:25.580
<b>even if it means enduring humiliating 
criticism and horrible compromises.</b>

11:26.300 --> 11:28.530
<b>We need to find a way out!</b>

11:29.100 --> 11:33.290
<b>We're going to win! 
Win an exit! Win the peace!</b>

11:34.270 --> 11:38.710
<b>Colonel, the military can only pass 
through an exit if it's an honorable one!</b>

11:38.710 --> 11:40.620
<b>The army's reputation is at stake!</b>

11:40.620 --> 11:43.000
<b>Or will you tell the fallen 
that they died for nothing?</b>

11:43.000 --> 11:45.670
<b>Could we really tell the Imperial 
family that this is our proposal?!</b>

11:45.670 --> 11:48.750
<b>An exit without victory is impossible!</b>

11:50.690 --> 11:54.180
<b>I see these conditions are 
worse than the previous ones.</b>

11:57.070 --> 11:59.780
<b>With each hour we squander, 
each opportunity we waste,</b>

11:59.780 --> 12:02.750
<b>the conditions we must accept get worse.</b>

12:03.270 --> 12:06.400
<b>Is time on our side, you think?</b>

12:06.400 --> 12:08.430
<b>We have yet to lose this war!</b>

12:09.030 --> 12:11.080
<b>Let's make the world admit...</b>

12:11.460 --> 12:15.160
<b>That we, the Imperial military, 
are the world's strongest power!</b>

12:16.070 --> 12:18.290
<b>But at the same time, 
we must admit to ourselves...</b>

12:18.290 --> 12:23.210
<b>That we were not quite strong enough 
to fight the whole world.</b>

12:25.490 --> 12:28.320
<b>Our fists may be scarred, 
but we can still land</b>

12:28.320 --> 12:30.600
<b>a hell of a punch on 
the rest of the world.</b>

12:31.150 --> 12:34.230
<b>But we're not strong enough 
to beat them to death.</b>

12:34.800 --> 12:37.520
<b>And if we miss the chance 
to our lower our fists,</b>

12:37.940 --> 12:41.580
<b>we'll be forced to fight 
until the very end.</b>

12:42.680 --> 12:45.220
<b>We have little time left.</b>

12:45.650 --> 12:49.440
<b>Isn't that why we have to find an exit?</b>

12:50.450 --> 12:56.090
<b>Before we fight the world, I believe 
we must put effort into our struggle.</b>

13:02.470 --> 13:08.020
<b>Diplomacy is like alchemy, in that
 you're creating something from nothing.</b>

13:09.030 --> 13:13.300
<b>The most important ingredient 
in that alchemy is trust.</b>

13:13.300 --> 13:15.770
<b>And its laws are all about fairness 
and equivalent exchange.</b>

13:15.770 --> 13:18.810
<b>Or at least, making sure both 
parties believe they exist.</b>

13:19.560 --> 13:24.650
<b>If war is the ultimate reality, 
diplomacy is the ultimate unreality.</b>

13:24.930 --> 13:29.220
<b>Multiple people can look at the same thing
 and interpret it in many different ways.</b>

13:29.570 --> 13:31.940
<b>It's not easy to come to an agreement.</b>

13:31.940 --> 13:35.070
<b>And sometimes, compromises 
may not be seen as such.</b>

13:35.580 --> 13:39.590
<b>And that's why a bold 
compromise is needed, but...</b>

13:39.590 --> 13:41.910
<b>An abandonment of demands for reparations</b>

13:41.910 --> 13:44.310
<b>and a de facto return to 
the prewar status quo.</b>

13:45.340 --> 13:48.970
<b>These are the best conditions 
the Empire can offer right now.</b>

13:49.460 --> 13:51.760
<b>Did the army really approve this?</b>

13:53.380 --> 13:54.410
<b>Yes.</b>

13:56.730 --> 13:59.440
<b>We're in sight of the goal!</b>

14:07.750 --> 14:14.740
<b><i>The Imperial army set out on two 
offensives, with a view to end the war.</i></b>

14:14.740 --> 14:19.880
<b><i>The stalemate in the east 
would be broken by a bold,</i></b>

14:19.880 --> 14:22.600
<b><i>highly mobile offensive 
led by General Zettour.</i></b>

14:22.600 --> 14:27.710
<b><i>A clear victory on the tactical level 
would be a show of the Empire's strength.</i></b>

14:28.150 --> 14:31.570
<b><i>And in the west, General Romel</i></b>

14:31.570 --> 14:35.670
<b><i>would lead a surprise assault 
on the Allied Kingdom homeland.</i></b>

14:35.670 --> 14:39.350
<b><i>A political offensive aimed at influencing
 public opinion in our enemy nations.</i></b>

14:39.350 --> 14:45.140
<b><i>But a chance encounter with 
an enemy fleet caused the plan to fail.</i></b>

14:45.140 --> 14:47.490
<b><i>Information leaks were suspected as well.</i></b>

14:47.730 --> 14:49.760
<b><i>It wasn't a perfect success.</i></b>

14:49.760 --> 14:53.990
<b><i>But the Empire felt it 
had landed a solid blow.</i></b>

14:54.470 --> 14:58.560
<b><i>The Empire hoped that if they 
could show their strength,</i></b>

14:58.560 --> 15:02.790
<b><i>they'd be able to drag their foes 
to the negotiating table.</i></b>

15:03.250 --> 15:06.250
<b>August 23rd, Unified Year 1927</b>

15:10.760 --> 15:13.760
<b>Ildoa Central Station</b>

15:37.130 --> 15:40.120
<b>General Gassman was terrified, you know.</b>

15:40.120 --> 15:42.340
<b>That she might be back to make 
another noisy entrance.</b>

15:42.890 --> 15:45.220
<b>My apologies to the general,</b>

15:45.220 --> 15:49.120
<b>but I hope we can get along with each 
other for the immediate future.</b>

15:50.140 --> 15:53.150
<b>It's like I'm talking to a diplomat.</b>

15:53.150 --> 15:58.510
<b>I'm a soldier. I'm acting this way 
because my homeland needs me to.</b>

15:59.580 --> 16:03.830
<b>Now, let me hear from you directly.</b>

16:03.830 --> 16:06.310
<b>What conditions can you offer?</b>

16:08.930 --> 16:11.010
<b><i>I've prepared something 
that will end this.</i></b>

16:17.440 --> 16:20.220
<b>No reparations. No territory changes.</b>

16:20.220 --> 16:23.080
<b>Rights for smaller ethnicities.
These are the three main pillars.</b>

16:24.610 --> 16:27.300
<b>Is that... possible?</b>

16:27.300 --> 16:30.750
<b>You really believe this can 
be done without reparations?</b>

16:31.030 --> 16:33.040
<b>You're right to be concerned.</b>

16:33.040 --> 16:35.920
<b>But the Empire will accept 
these conditions.</b>

16:37.920 --> 16:42.690
<b>I'm sorry. Did you say "accept"?</b>

16:42.690 --> 16:43.850
<b>Yes.</b>

16:43.850 --> 16:46.180
<b>We're prepared to accept this.</b>

16:46.530 --> 16:50.060
<b>Just in case, let me get this straight...</b>

16:50.500 --> 16:56.680
<b>When you say no reparations, you 
mean you won't ask for reparations,</b>

16:56.680 --> 17:00.800
<b>not that you're refusing demands 
for them from your enemies?</b>

17:01.430 --> 17:03.440
<b>That's correct. Why?</b>

17:04.950 --> 17:08.680
<b>So you have no intention of 
paying reparations, then?</b>

17:11.840 --> 17:15.090
<b>Us? Pay reparations?</b>

17:20.770 --> 17:22.090
<b>I-Impossible!</b>

17:22.350 --> 17:25.300
<b>We're abandoning our 
demands for reparations!</b>

17:25.300 --> 17:28.880
<b>Are you saying that even a huge 
compromise like this isn't enough?</b>

17:30.090 --> 17:35.350
<b>So you're saying you won't be 
handing over Imperial territory?</b>

17:37.120 --> 17:42.170
<b>Colonel Rerugen, to be honest...</b>

17:42.540 --> 17:45.380
<b>Your proposal will likely 
be taken as a provocation.</b>

17:45.990 --> 17:47.680
<b>But why?</b>

17:47.680 --> 17:50.200
<b>You refuse to hand over 
territory or pay reparations.</b>

17:50.570 --> 17:54.130
<b>From the perspective of your enemies, 
this is a clear provocation.</b>

17:58.610 --> 18:03.570
<b>The Empire sees it as a shameful proposal 
we're accepting for the sake of peace...</b>

18:03.950 --> 18:07.970
<b>But a third party would see it 
as an insulting provocation?</b>

18:10.710 --> 18:13.700
<b>We live in entirely different worlds...</b>

18:17.490 --> 18:19.110
<b>Colonel Calandro,</b>

18:19.110 --> 18:22.770
<b>I'm sure you're aware that war started</b>

18:22.770 --> 18:25.570
<b>when the Entente Alliance 
violated our borders!</b>

18:26.010 --> 18:27.170
<b>That's right.</b>

18:27.170 --> 18:28.780
<b>They started it.</b>

18:28.780 --> 18:32.830
<b>We simply protected ourselves 
in a fight they started!</b>

18:32.830 --> 18:35.340
<b>I'm sure they'd see it differently.</b>

18:35.830 --> 18:40.400
<b>For instance, the Empire was 
the first to declare war.</b>

18:40.400 --> 18:42.530
<b>The first to fire shots, too.</b>

18:42.530 --> 18:43.620
<b>But that's absurd!</b>

18:43.620 --> 18:47.600
<b>We exercised our clear right to 
self-defense against a border violation!</b>

18:47.600 --> 18:50.550
<b>Yes. The Empire feels 
it was in the right.</b>

18:50.910 --> 18:54.860
<b>But other nations see 
the matter differently.</b>

18:56.610 --> 18:59.890
<b>I want you to understand that 
negotiations aren't possible</b>

18:59.890 --> 19:03.750
<b>unless the Empire is willing 
to offer serious concessions.</b>

19:03.750 --> 19:06.310
<b>That's how your enemies see this.</b>

19:07.490 --> 19:12.210
<b>They're willing to continue the war, 
even if we offer these conditions?</b>

19:12.210 --> 19:15.660
<b>I'm sorry, but too much 
blood has been shed.</b>

19:15.660 --> 19:19.250
<b>Your enemies can't go home 
empty-handed either.</b>

19:21.050 --> 19:23.780
<b>So we have to keep fighting?</b>

19:29.370 --> 19:34.870
<b>Is it truly impossible for we and 
our enemies to come together,</b>

19:34.870 --> 19:36.890
<b>in the name of restoring peace?</b>

19:38.770 --> 19:42.990
<b>Colonel Rerugen, you're a loyal soldier.</b>

19:42.990 --> 19:47.160
<b>In light of that, may I 
give my personal opinion?</b>

19:49.440 --> 19:51.080
<b>Essentially...</b>

19:52.030 --> 19:53.870
<b>The Empire is too powerful.</b>

19:53.870 --> 19:55.420
<b>Too powerful, and too scary.</b>

19:55.420 --> 19:58.930
<b>And we wish to see the thing 
which scares us destroyed.</b>

20:26.680 --> 20:30.880
<b><i>It hurts to be the one who 
sits at home, waiting.</i></b>

20:53.350 --> 20:57.730
<b>Lieutenant Colonel, Strategic HQ 
has sent you a sealed message.</b>

20:59.170 --> 21:01.640
<b>Damn it! This is...</b>

21:02.800 --> 21:04.990
<b>Things are as bad 
as they could possibly be.</b>

21:04.990 --> 21:07.250
<b>How truly wonderful.</b>

21:08.630 --> 21:11.530
<b>We can make an exit for 
ourselves after all.</b>

21:11.530 --> 21:13.040
<b>Impossible.</b>

21:13.040 --> 21:17.320
<b>This leaves us with no choice.</b>

21:16.160 --> 21:18.920
No hope in diplomatic efforts

21:21.710 --> 21:23.190
<b><i>We're out of time.</i></b>

21:24.890 --> 21:27.970
<b><i>Our fists are still strong.</i></b>

21:30.080 --> 21:32.450
<b><i>We can still land a punch on the world.</i></b>

21:32.880 --> 21:37.240
<b><i>But at some point, 
even if we invade Ildoa...</i></b>

21:38.190 --> 21:40.390
<b><i>It won't lead us to an exit.</i></b>

21:40.900 --> 21:42.920
<b><i>But if we don't punch now...</i></b>

21:43.340 --> 21:47.240
<b><i>If we lose our ability to even do that...</i></b>

21:48.400 --> 21:52.630
<b><i>What will the world do to the Empire?</i></b>

22:06.010 --> 22:10.010
<b>Next Time
Hourglass</b>
